 34NE c  Two independent experiments have been done, one at RIKEN and the other 
 34NE2c  at GANIL using two different {+48}Ca beam energies. In each, two events
 34NE3c  were assigned to {+34}Ne nuclide.                                      
 34NE c  2002No11 (also 2002Lu19): {+34}Ne seen in reaction: Ta({+48}Ca,X) E=64 
 34NE2c  MeV/nucleon. Reaction fragments analyzed by RIPS recoil fragment       
 34NE3c  separator at RIKEN facility. Identification by measurements of energy  
 34NE4c  loss, total kinetic energy, time-of-flight and magnetic rigidity for   
 34NE5c  each fragment. Measured |s|?0.1 pb for yield of {+34}Ne in the above   
 34NE6c  reaction corresponding to two events seen in 2002No11 (also 2002Lu19)  
 34NE c  2004Lu19, 2003Lu11, 2002Lu19, 2002Lu09: RIKEN-GANIL-Dubna              
 34NE2c  collaboration. {+34}Ne confirmed in reaction: Ta({+48}Ca,X) E=58.9     
 34NE3c  MeV/nucleon. Fragmentation of {+48}Ca primary beam. Reaction fragments 
 34NE4c  analyzed by RIPS recoil fragment separator at RIKEN facility and       
 34NE5c  LISE-2000 spectrometer at GANIL. Isotopic identification by            
 34NE6c  measurements of energy loss, total kinetic energy, time-of-flight and  
 34NE7c  magnetic rigidity for each fragment. Two events (see figure 1a of      
 34NE8c  2002No11 or figure 1b of 2002Lu19) were observed for {+34}Ne with      
 34NE9c  measured |s=0.17 pb {I12} for {+34}Ne in GANIL experiment              
